    "notes": "Inspected53 current frames:12 portable,12 shared-material/flat-map and29 Earth-rig/tier views. Six-lane roadway, pale four-plate-girder river unit, broad transverse concrete piers, longer land approaches, lower separate paths, west bank bends, east path loop, rails, median and slender paired-arm lights remain coherent. Source retains dense railing pickets; browser tiers aggregate them and far tiers omit furniture. Main girder unit is423m, not stretched to the866m mapped full viaduct. Signed lower-path ramps follow the standard PMTiles extract. Three shared concrete/coated-metal/aggregate graphs use metric UVs; palette paint and no private images. Default whole-crossing/context views are too distant for fine detail; authored road/path/underside cameras provide that inspection. Flat synthetic ground does not prove native bank contact; coarse terrain samples and the PMTiles plan supply the approximate fit. Some High shadow maps show repeated thin-geometry shadow aliasing on the long road/girder; portable geometry and deck ray checks show no missing panels. Reconstructed pier/approach spacing, unsurveyed water datum, ramp grades/contacts, representative service pipes and unmeasured physical-device performance remain explicit."
  },
